#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:5
#: 4793839a4a264250a08493898085c229
msgid "PWM, OneShot and OneShot125 ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:7
#: 8b2d1320cdd548aca78aabe8897c08cb
msgid "Most ArduPilot vehicles use brushless motors controlled by brushless motor ESCs. The most common protocols used by these ESCs are PWM, OneShot, OneShot125, and :ref:`DShot <common-dshot-escs>`. This page describes the first three (PWM, OneShot and OneShot125)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:9
#: b0358b2e8e91442c92711d9bce18fe8b
msgid "Be sure your ESC can support the configuration you select for it. Damage can occur otherwise. This includes frame rates discussed below. Also be careful when switching between protocols without rebooting or re-calibrating ESCs as this can lead to uncommanded motor output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:12
#: 7cf04602267d4328867404c76bc8222c
msgid "PWM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:13
#: c13bea75c75b42c89618eea3a987ba7d
msgid "These are the most common ESCs for non-copter applications and were historically the first brushless ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:17
#: ddaa034514844aa38495f870e5e46e55
msgid "PWM ESCs use a periodic input pulse of width typically between 1000uS and 2000uS for zero to full power, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:21
#: cef8b2b4878749b6912487122746463e
msgid "Set :ref:`MOT_PWM_TYPE <MOT_PWM_TYPE>` to 0/Normal (the default) and reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:22
#: fa649a7972f5471d8747bb6a3a9ec079
msgid "The PWM range for each channel is specified by the corresponding :ref:`SERVOx_MIN <SERVO3_MIN>` and :ref:`SERVOx_MAX <SERVO3_MAX>` parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:26
#: d6efc58dad3248df8dd9665eebbd6f30
msgid "The frame rate of these pulses is usually between 50Hz to 490Hz. The faster frame rates allow quicker control reactions to be sent to the motor, if the ESC has capability for those frame rates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:30
#: 56a880c19172445890c1c54eb7d45eb1
msgid "Set :ref:`SERVO_RATE <SERVO_RATE>` to change the frame rate (default is 50Hz)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:34
#: 52c56071caa84972a5711d881e3c6d43
msgid "be sure of the capabilities of your ESC before selecting a higher frame rate to avoid damage to the ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:37
#: 80cb7cce0e7b409d89089bd963ec1566
msgid "OneShot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:39
#: b4ca9dbd2506454fabc0663d2e7c36aa
msgid "OneShot (not to be confused with \"OneShot125\") is an older protocol that uses the same pulse widths as Normal PWM but has a fixed frame rate equal to the autopilot main loop rate.  There is little advantage for using this protocol over regular PWM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:42
#: d72a75152ea64699b756fd5549285830
msgid "Set :ref:`MOT_PWM_TYPE <MOT_PWM_TYPE>` to 1 (OneShot) and reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:47
#: 1cb9f65d017244fbbbe05f8243765205
msgid "OneShot 125"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:49
#: cc6a3c06d4b44134bf2c66738b6ef4ad
msgid "The OneShot125 (sometimes confusingly shortened to just OneShot) protocol is similar to regular PWM except that the pulse widths are divided by a factor of 8 which allows faster communication from the autopilot to the ESC.  Individual pulses are sent more quickly and the overall frame rate can be increased up to 490Hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:52
#: 74b0893321e447ecbf2407cbb789db28
msgid "Set :ref:`MOT_PWM_TYPE <MOT_PWM_TYPE>` to 2 (OneShot125) and reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:56
#: aa0ec0ef973444febe805d6f14c02793
msgid "If using an autopilot with an IOMCU (e.g. Pixhawk, CubeOrange) the ESCs should be connected to the AUX outputs and the corresponding :ref:`SERVOx_FUNCTION <SERVO9_FUNCTION>` values should be set to \"Motor1\", etc.  This can be most easily done using Mission Planner's \"Servo Output\" page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:60
#: 89d27092361c4285b76eb6160d5e11fb
msgid "Reboot the autopilot and check the \"RC banner\" to confirm the output channels are setup as expected (this banner appears whenever parameters are downloaded)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:67
#: c0569ec5e8dc4f51be9fbf298ffa21c0
msgid "Mixing ESC Protocols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:69
#: 7fc86497f1114de1aed5169159135c0d
msgid "While all the servo/motor outputs of an ArduPilot autopilot are capable of Normal PWM operation at 50Hz frame rates, not all are capable of other ESC protocols. And, usually, these configurations must apply to pre-designated groups of outputs, even if they are not all driving an ESC. So the following cautions apply:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:71
#: 8c8727a67eed4e37a8ebe4cdd5e54aa2
msgid "The 8 \"MAIN\" outputs of autopilots using an IOMCU (like PixHawk and Cube), cannot be used for  protocols other than Normal PWM and OneShot. On these autopilots, only the additional \"AUX\" outputs can properly support OneShot125. If you attempt to set a \"MAIN\" output to OneShot125, then normal PWM output will occur, even though it has been set to a OneShot125 protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:73
#: a9172653b7e545da8680c1f4427c4978
msgid "For :ref:`Pixracer <common-pixracer-overview>` and :ref:`other boards <common-autopilots>` without a separate IOMCU coprocessor, all servo/motor outputs can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:75
#: b0c537dd3260410a9849ca3a0e78b7db
msgid "Groups of outputs sharing a common timer, MUST have the same advanced configuration. Usually, these are specified in the autopilot's hardware description linked from the :ref:`common-autopilots` page. For example, if an output is configured for OneShot125 in a group, then you cannot use another output in that group for Normal PWM ESC **or** normal PWM servo operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-brushless-escs.rst:77
#: 2bae6bb8569241a3820c7960a1c4db8f
msgid "Every time the autopilot initializes, it sends the \"RC Banner\" to the ground control station, showing which outputs are PWM, OneShot, OneShot125 or DShot. The remaining higher numbered outputs are assigned as GPIOs."
msgstr ""
